🧩 1. Access Layers (The 7‑Layer Access Stack)
Access operates across seven layers, each with its own rules:

Layer 1 — Relic‑Anchored Access
Access granted by owning specific relics.

Layer 2 — Token‑Anchored Access
Access granted by staking or burning tokens.

Layer 3 — Dataset Access
Access granted by dataset relics or dataset licenses.

Layer 4 — Innovation Access
Access granted by innovation relics or cycle participation.

Layer 5 — Enterprise Access
Access granted by enterprise relics or enterprise contracts.

Layer 6 — Season Access
Access granted by season relics or seasonal participation.

Layer 7 — Contribution Access
Access granted by creator status, lineage depth, or cycle completion.

Each layer can override or reinforce the others.

